*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
.qoder/
__pycache__/
node_modules/

# python test artifacts
.coverage
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

docs/

# the tasklist-first guard's portable satisfier — per-phase working state, not a
# deliverable, and it carries a nonce that is meaningless outside its session
/.claude/tasklist.md
# machine-local hook state. The fixed hooks write these to ~/.claude/plc-state/<repo>/
# instead, so on a current plugin build these paths are never created — but a session running an
# OLDER cached build still writes them here, and an unignored file dirties the tree, which is one
# of close-gate-nudge.sh's own trigger conditions. Observed live minutes after the fix commit:
# both stamps reappeared as `??` and the hook then warned about "uncommitted changes" that were
# its own two writes. Kept as a permanent floor rather than removed once everyone upgrades — two
# lines, against a failure that is silent.
/.claude/.close-gate-nudge-last
/.claude/.clear-nudge-last
/.claude/.gate-runs/

# session-local resume artifact (never publish)
# NB: anchor to root so only the top-level RESUME.md is ignored — an unanchored
# `RESUME.md` matches any nested path of that name on case-insensitive filesystems
# (macOS APFS) and could wrongly ignore a shipped file. (Historically this collided
# with the old `commands/resume.md`, since renamed to `commands/recall.md`.)
/RESUME.md
# cold sibling written by /handoff (archive-before-overwrite) — holds verbatim
# outgoing snapshots incl. cross-project identifiers; never publish.
/RESUME-archive.md

# local embedding-model cache (ONNX weights etc.) pulled by dev tooling — a large
# binary blob, never part of the skill deliverable; keep it out of history.
/local_cache/
